        "text_iYVVL8": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<h2>Gathering Nectar</h2><p>Bees use their straw-like tongues to suck nectar from flowers, storing it in their specialized “honey stomach” for the journey back to the hive.</p><h2>Transforming & Dehydrating</h2><p>Bees use their straw-like tongues to suck nectar from flowers, storing it in their specialized “honey stomach” for the journey back to the hive.</p><h2>Harvesting & Jarring</h2><p>When cells are capped with wax (indicating the honey is ripe), beekeepers harvest the frames, remove the wax caps, extract the honey (e.g., by spinning), filter it, and pour it into jars</p>",
            "text_style": "body"
          }
        }
